  "what_this_is": "The varsity programs each school sponsors. The item reviewer names an item's subject from these keys rather than inventing a label, so that the same program is never recorded two ways. Keys are <school>/<program>; a bare <school> key means the athletics department as a whole, and 'conference' means the Pac-12 itself. Those three depths are one key space.",
  "how_it_was_built": "Seven schools scraped from their own sport navigation on 2026-09-06, one request each. Washington State's and Texas State's navs are JavaScript-rendered and return nothing to a plain fetch; the CEO supplied both lists from those sites' teams pages. Program slugs and labels are each school's own, not normalised — schools differ (one lists 'cross-country', another 'womens-cross-country'), and inventing a common vocabulary is a separate job that nothing needs yet.",
  "when_a_team_is_missing": "The reviewer records the raw string in 'unrecognized' rather than dropping it, so a gap in this file surfaces as a queue rather than as silent loss. Adding a program is a one-line edit here; items already judged keep the key they were given, because the verdict log is forward-only.",
